# Review routing. A team, never an individual: the point of this file is that
# it keeps working when any one person stops maintaining the project.
#
# Ownership here only *requests* a review. "Require review from Code Owners"
# is deliberately off in branch protection - with a small maintainer group it
# would mean nobody could merge anything. See GOVERNANCE.md.

*                       @sinceaihq/engineering

# Changing what a verdict means is the one category that should never be a
# quiet merge. Scoring constants, rule severities and the rule set itself
# decide whether someone ships or does not ship.
/src/rules/             @sinceaihq/engineering
/src/scoring/           @sinceaihq/engineering

# The analysis foundation. A lexer bug is not local: it silently moves every
# position in every report, which is how the 1.0.0 line-number bug survived.
/src/analysis/          @sinceaihq/engineering

# Supply chain. These decide what gets published, with what permissions, and
# what a workflow pinned to @v1 actually executes.
/.github/workflows/     @sinceaihq/engineering
/action/                @sinceaihq/engineering
/scripts/               @sinceaihq/engineering
/package.json           @sinceaihq/engineering

# The promises. SECURITY.md and the threat model are load-bearing claims.
/SECURITY.md            @sinceaihq/engineering
/GOVERNANCE.md          @sinceaihq/engineering
/docs/THREAT_MODEL.md   @sinceaihq/engineering
